{"tool_name":"corset","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"corset","version":"1.09","home":"https://github.com/Oshlack/Corset","documentation":"https://github.com/Oshlack/Corset/wiki","license":"GPL-3.0-or-later","summary":"Software for clustering de novo assembled transcripts and counting overlapping reads.","identifiers":["biotools:corset","doi:10.1186/s13059-014-0410-6"],"build":{"number":6,"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"build":["make",null,"autoconf","automake","libtool","pkg-config","gnuconfig"],"host":["zlib","samtools 0.1.19"],"run":["samtools 0.1.19"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/Oshlack/Corset/archive/version-1.09.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["corset 2>&1 | grep \"Usage\""]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"corset","identifiers":["biotools:corset","doi:10.1186/s13059-014-0410-6"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Software for clustering de novo assembled transcripts and counting overlapping reads.","home_url":"https://github.com/Oshlack/Corset","keywords":["Animals","Chick Embryo","Cluster Analysis","Humans","Models, Statistical","Sequence Analysis, RNA","Transcriptome","Yeasts","Omics","Clustering"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"corset","home":"https://github.com/Oshlack/Corset/wiki","summary":"Command-line software program to go from a de novo transcriptome assembly to gene-level counts. This software takes a set of reads that have been multi-mapped to the transcriptome and hierarchically clusters the transcripts based on the proportion of shared reads and expression patterns. It will report the clusters and gene-level counts for each sample, which are easily tested for differential expression with count based tools such as edgeR and DESeq.","addition_date":"2016-08-17T12:00:51Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:52Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["1"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:corset","credit":[{"email":"nadia.davidson@mcri.edu.au","name":"Australia","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"unimelb.edu.au","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/Oshlack/Corset/wiki"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2945"}]}],"name":"Corset","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"mv.schneider@unimelb.edu.au","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-014-0410-6","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2014 Davidson and Oshlack; licensee BioMed Central Ltd.Next generation sequencing has made it possible to perform differential gene expression studies in non-model organisms. For these studies, the need for a reference genome is circumvented by performing de novo assembly on the RNA-seq data. However, transcriptome assembly produces a multitude of contigs, which must be clustered into genes prior to differential gene expression detection. Here we present Corset, a method that hierarchically clusters contigs using shared reads and expression, then summarizes read counts to clusters, ready for statistical testing. Using a range of metrics, we demonstrate that Corset out-performs alternative methods.","authors":[{"name":"Davidson N.M."},{"name":"Oshlack A."}],"citationCount":227,"date":"2014-07-26T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Biology","title":"Corset: Enabling differential gene expression analysis for de novo assembled transcriptomes"},"type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Omics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3391"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Corset","home":"https://bio.tools/corset","version":"1","summary":"Command-line software program to go from a de novo transcriptome assembly to gene-level counts. This software takes a set of reads that have been multi-mapped to the transcriptome and hierarchically clusters the transcripts based on the proportion of shared reads and expression patterns. It will report the clusters and ge